```text
FINANCE COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Finance Committee was held on Monday, December 4, 2023, in Committee
Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Jeff White, Chairman, Dr. Michelle Aldrich, Ken Esquibel, and
Scott Roybal.
AGENDA ITEMS
6.
ORDINANCE 3” READING
— Creating Section 12.04.240, Mobile Storage Containers
on Public Right-of-Way; Peniiit Required, of Chapter 12.04, Streets, Sidewalks and
Driveways Generally, of Title 12, Streets, Sidewalks and Public Places, of the Municipal
Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming and making a conforming amendment as
specified. (POSTPONED FROM NOVEMBER 27, 2023)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. Roybal.
Dr. Aldrich
moved to amend by substitute dated November 21, 2023, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion to
amend carried with Dr. Aldrich and Mr. Esquibel voting “YES” and Mr. Roybal voting “NO”. Dr.
Aldrich moved to amend in paragraphs (D)( I) and (D)(2) to remove the language specifying when
a renewed permit would begin to toll—’from the date of the initial [or first] permit renewal
expiration”, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion to amend carried by unanimous voice vote. Main
motion, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote.
John Brodie, Deputy City Attorney, provided a staff report and committee member Aldrich
commented on the item.
25.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing a three (3) percent cost-of-living salary adjustment for all
permanent full and part-time employees of the City of Cheyenne. (SPONSOR
— MR.
WHITE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Mayor Patrick Collins provided an overview of the proposed cost-of-living salary adjustments and
Robin Lockman, City Treasurer, provided additional infonnation. Committee members Aldrich
and Roybal commented on the item.
26.
RESOLUTION
— Permitting the possession of open containers within the Downtown
District Boundaries for New Years Eve on December 31, 2023.
(SPONSOR
— MR.
JOHNSON)
Mr. Roybal moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Esquibel.
Motion carried with Mr. Esquibel and
Mr. Roybal voting “YES” and Dr. Aldrich voting ‘NO”.
```

